menu "RL policy on the robot (mpx_policy)"

    config MP4_POLICY_ENABLE
        bool "Run RL walk policies on the ESP32-S3 (`policy` console command)"
        default y

    config MP4_POLICY_ROBOT
        string "This robot (a policy for another one needs `force`)"
        default "sku1"
        depends on MP4_POLICY_ENABLE
        help
            Compared with the robot named in a policy file. A policy trained
            on another robot's model (another body, other servos) can do
            anything on this one, so it does not start without `force`.

    config MP4_POLICY_INTERNAL_RESERVE_KB
        int "Keep the network in internal RAM if this much (KB) stays free"
        default 96
        range 0 1024
        depends on MP4_POLICY_ENABLE
        help
            The network's weights (about 130 KB) are read in full at every
            50 Hz step. From internal RAM that takes well under a
            millisecond; from PSRAM several. The policy goes to internal
            RAM when, after it, at least this much internal RAM is still
            free (Wi-Fi, TLS and the tasks need it); otherwise to PSRAM.
            0: always PSRAM.

endmenu
